{
  "slug": "sf2a-vignettes",
  "name": "Two ways of noticing",
  "questionnaire_type": "composable",
  "instructions": "People notice things in different ways. Our brains can toggle between two modes: a doing mode, which is goal-directed and uses knowledge we already have, and a sensing mode, which explores our sensory world to discover new things.\n\nIn the doing mode, we look or listen to find something, like our keys, or to check that all is well, like a body ache or a strange sound outside. In the sensing mode, we look, listen, smell, taste or feel just out of curiosity, taking in whatever is there. Everyone does both at times, and neither is better. There are no right or wrong answers.",
